.\" sball-rollout manual page
.TH SBALL-ROLLOUT 8 "2026-10-14" "sball-addition 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sball-rollout \- quorum safe, one node at a time rollout of sball-addition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sball-rollout
\fB\-\-nodes=\fIfile\fR|\fIhost1,host2\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B sball-rollout
\fB\-\-local\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sball-rollout
installs or updates sball-addition on a PVM cluster over ssh, one node at a
time, and waits for every node to become quorate again before it continues. Per
node it performs:
.IP "1." 3
check whether sball-addition is installed and print the version
.IP "2." 3
copy and install the artifact
.RB ( "rpm \-Uvh"
for
.IR \-\-rpm ,
or extraction plus
.I scripts/install.sh
for
.IR \-\-tarball )
.IP "3." 3
.B sball-addition validate
\(em a broken hook set aborts the node before the service is touched
.IP "4." 3
.B systemctl daemon-reload
and
.B systemctl restart sballd.service
.IP "5." 3
wait for quorate by polling
.BR "sball-addition watcher \-\-once"
.IP "6." 3
.B sball-node-verify
(with
.B \-\-smoke
when requested)
.PP
Nodes are ordered so that the cluster master is rolled out last, which is
detected by asking every node
.BR "sball-addition status" .
The rollout stops at the first failure unless
.B \-\-continue\-on\-error
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Target selection
.TP
.BI \-\-nodes= spec
A file with one host per line (blank lines and
.B #
comments are ignored) or a comma separated list.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Roll out on this machine only, without ssh.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the resolved order and exit. Combine with
.B \-\-nodes
to review the plan.
.SS Artifact
.TP
.BI \-\-rpm= file
Copy this RPM and install it with
.BR "rpm \-Uvh \-\-replacepkgs" .
.TP
.BI \-\-tarball= file
Copy this tarball, extract it under
.I /tmp
and run its
.IR scripts/install.sh " \-\-with\-systemd" .
.SS Behaviour
.TP
.BI \-\-wait\-quorate= seconds
How long to wait for a node to report quorate again (default 300).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-master\-last
Keep the given order; do not move the master node to the end.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-restart
Install and verify only; never restart
.BR sballd.service .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Skip
.B sball-node-verify
at the end of each node.
.TP
.B \-\-smoke
Pass
.B \-\-smoke
to
.BR sball-node-verify ,
so every node runs a temporary hook.
.TP
.B \-\-continue\-on\-error
Keep going after a node failed (the exit status still reports the failure).
.TP
.BI \-\-maintenance= text
Reason shown in the log lines (for example a change ticket id).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-user= user
Login name for ssh/scp (default root, or
.BR $SBALL_SSH_USER ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-port= port
ssh port (default 22, or
.BR $SBALL_SSH_PORT ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-opt= "options"
Extra options passed to ssh and scp (or
.BR $SBALL_SSH_OPTS ).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan and every command that would run, and execute nothing. Always
run this first.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show the output of every remote command.
.SH INTERACTION
When
.B \-\-dry\-run
is not given and the service will be restarted, the command asks for a typed
.B yes
on a terminal before it touches the first node.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every node was rolled out and verified
.TP
.B 1
at least one node failed, or the rollout was stopped early
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.SH EXAMPLES
Review the order (master last) without doing anything:
.PP
.RS
sball-rollout \-\-nodes=nodes.txt \-\-list
.RE
.PP
Full rollout with checksums verified artifacts:
.PP
.RS
sball-rollout \-\-nodes=nodes.txt \-\-rpm=/root/sball-addition-1.0.0-1.x86_64.rpm \\
              \-\-maintenance="CHG-12345" \-\-smoke
.RE
.PP
Safe migration where no restart is allowed:
.PP
.RS
sball-rollout \-\-nodes=nodes.txt \-\-rpm=/root/sball-addition.rpm \-\-no\-restart
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sball-addition (8),
.BR sball-node-verify (8),
.BR sballd-wrapper (8),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
